  "created": "2021-08-05T18:14:58.722Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Having the VRCSDK3-WORLD-2021.08.04.15.07 Control Panel visible in Unity 2019.4.29f1 causes Unity process to eat up an entire CPU core (and then some more).\nHowever despite that, it doesn't seem laggy or slow.\nIt doesn't matter whether you're logged in to it.\nIt doesn't matter which CP tab is visible.\nIt doesn't matter if it's side-by-side with Inspector like in my example, or free-floating, or anywhere else.\nIt seems that when visible, Unity is redrawing it multiple times per second.\nIt happens even in a freshly-created empty project with just SDK imported.\nIt did not happen in Unity 2018 with latest (for that version) SDK version.",
